   "subject": "msaplot error in shiny--no package called 'Biostrings'",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Dear Guangchuang Yu and co-authors,</div><div><br></div><div>I am having an issue using ggtree in a Shiny app. The app was supposed to call msaplot, which I believe calls read.fasta from treeio, which in turn calls<span><span>&quot;</span>readBStringSet<span>&quot;</span></span> from Biostrings. Unfortunately, there is an issue loading Biostrings. Here is the relevant output from my Shiny web app log:  <br> </div><div><br></div><div><pre>Loading required package: Biostrings\r\n2018-10-24T19:54:42.136213+00:00 shinyapps[463434]:   there is no package called ‘Biostrings’\r\n2018-10-24T19:54:42.142083+00:00 shinyapps[463434]:   62: read.fasta\r\n2018-10-24T19:54:42.136956+00:00 shinyapps[463434]: Warning: Error in eval: object &#39;readBStringSet&#39; not found<br><br><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Note that when I use a normal ggtree plot this error does not occur. Only with msaplot. I don&#39;t see Biostrings listed on the Imports or </span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Depends lists in the treeio package--could this be causing this issue?<br><br>Many thanks for your help. I&#39;d love to get this sorted and use the msaplot function in my app. <br></span><br></pre></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ht7Rh8IiCQAJ",
   "from": "Yu, Guangchuang",
   "author": "cec41188340e8212",
   "date": "2018-10-29T01:45:18Z",
   "subject": "Re: msaplot error in shiny--no package called 'Biostrings'",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Yes, you are right.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">You can fix the issue by explicitly load the <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">Biostrings</code> package before calling <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">msaplot</code>.</p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">On Thu, Oct 25, 2018 at 4:22 AM <a href=\"http://mailto:dle...@gmail.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mailto:dle...@gmail.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482397097000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3KNhH6UY0MqFmjFrGJjpmD\">dlevy...@gmail.com</a> wrote:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Dear Guangchuang Yu and co-authors,</div><div><br></div><div>I am having an issue using ggtree in a Shiny app. The app was supposed to call msaplot, which I believe calls read.fasta from treeio, which in turn calls<span><span>&quot;</span>readBStringSet<span>&quot;</span></span> from Biostrings. Unfortunately, there is an issue loading Biostrings. Here is the relevant output from my Shiny web app log:  <br> </div><div><br></div><div><pre>Loading required package: Biostrings\r\n2018-10-24T19:54:42.136213+00:00 shinyapps[463434]:   there is no package called ‘Biostrings’\r\n2018-10-24T19:54:42.142083+00:00 shinyapps[463434]:   62: read.fasta\r\n2018-10-24T19:54:42.136956+00:00 shinyapps[463434]: Warning: Error in eval: object &#39;readBStringSet&#39; not found<br><br><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Note that when I use a normal ggtree plot this error does not occur. Only with msaplot. I don&#39;t see Biostrings listed on the Imports or </span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Depends lists in the treeio package--could this be causing this issue?<br><br>Many thanks for your help. I&#39;d love to get this sorted and use the msaplot function in my app. <br></span><br></pre></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
